From: OpenWrt scratch debug
Subject: DEBUG: net: airoha: disable FE VIP force-to-CPU for PPPoE Discovery

DEBUG-only diagnostic patch, part of an investigation into a silent
DHCP-reply receive loss on the Nokia XG-040G-MF (Airoha AN7583).

airoha_fe_vip_setup() force-routes PPPoE Discovery frames (ethertype
0x8863, REG_FE_VIP_PATN(3)) onto the same hardware "force to CPU"
classification path (PATN_FCPU_EN_MASK, RX queue 4 via
REG_CDM_FWD_CFG CDM_VIP_QSEL_MASK=0x4) as BOOTP (see the companion
926-DEBUG-an7583-disable-bootp-vip-fcpu.patch in this series).

This is untested against an actual PPPoE/BRAS reproduction - it is
offered as a candidate experiment for anyone who can reproduce
openwrt/openwrt#24715 (PPPoE PADO never arriving from the BRAS on
this same board after the first ~2 minutes), based on the working
hypothesis that both symptoms share the same underlying FE VIP
force-to-CPU mechanism, just triggered on different traffic classes.
Removing PATN_FCPU_EN_MASK from the BOOTP entries (926) has shown a
DHCP-reply loss-free run well past the previous consistent 36-45
minute failure window in early testing; this patch applies the
identical technique to the PPPoE Discovery entry to see whether it
similarly avoids the PADO loss. Not a confirmed fix either way.

Not for upstream submission - diagnostic-only, changes hardware
classification behavior for PPPoE Discovery traffic.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -201,7 +201,8 @@
 static void airoha_fe_vip_setup(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 {
 	airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_FE_VIP_PATN(3), ETH_P_PPP_DISC);
-	airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_FE_VIP_EN(3), PATN_FCPU_EN_MASK | PATN_EN_MASK);
+	/* DEBUG: force-to-CPU intentionally disabled here */
+	airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_FE_VIP_EN(3), PATN_EN_MASK);
 
 	airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_FE_VIP_PATN(4), PPP_LCP);
 	airoha_fe_wr(eth, REG_FE_VIP_EN(4),
